## Frequently Asked Questions

### What format is the guide?

The guide is delivered as a digital PDF through Gumroad. You can access it after purchasing and keep it for personal reference.

### How long does the fertility cycle take?

The central ritual system is organised into four months, with each month devoted to a different stage: Opening, Warming, Calling and Sustaining.

The guide also contains additional practices outside the central cycle.

### Do I need to follow the moon phases?

Moon phases are included as traditional symbolic timing. They are not strict requirements. The guide also discusses beginning in relation to the menstrual cycle and adapting the practices to individual circumstances.

### Does the guide include herbal recipes?

Yes. The herbal section explores traditional plants and includes several tea blend recipes with ingredients and preparation instructions.

These are traditional and symbolic preparations, not clinically established fertility treatments. Herbal ingredients can have contraindications, particularly when trying to conceive or during pregnancy. Seek advice from a qualified healthcare professional before consuming these preparations.

### What if I have experienced pregnancy loss?

The guide includes a separate three-week folk restoration cycle devoted to remembrance, grief and new beginnings. It is a symbolic spiritual resource, not a substitute for medical care or grief counselling.

### What if I become pregnant during the four-month cycle?

The guide provides a transition into its Protection After Conception section. Conception rituals should not be continued as though the original cycle still applies.

### Will the rituals help me become pregnant?

This guide explores traditional beliefs, symbolism and spiritual practices. It does not claim to increase conception rates, treat infertility, prevent miscarriage or guarantee pregnancy. It is not a medical fertility programme or a substitute for medical assessment and treatment.

